<title>UK: Reckitt down as bid hopes fade.</title>
<headline>Reckitt down as bid hopes fade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Reckitt &amp; Colman Plc fell on Thursday, retreating from Wednesday's peak as bid fever cooled following market rumours that Unilever Plc would instead bid for French food group Danone, dealers said.</p>
<p>Reckitt shares were down 17p at 808 by 1300 GMT, after rising on Wednesday to as high as 837p -- up from 709-1/2p on February 10, the day before Unilever sparked bid speculation by saying it planned to sell its speciality chemical unit to focus on consumer brands.</p>
<p>Unilever declined comment on the latest market rumours, which lifted Danone shares 2.2 percent to 881 francs in Paris.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
